db/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087939 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186051028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087939 #edb/ref 1050 540.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087939 #edb/ref 1050 540.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186087939 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "32fc74f9-ca5f-5f57-a626-d4e31a145f67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087977 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186084596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087977 #edb/ref 1069 "q-10483" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087977 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087977 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087977 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bb5b26cc-aa49-5ffc-81f1-0bc5ef548212" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087977 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\pm 2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087978 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186084602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087978 #edb/ref 1069 "q-10489" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087978 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087978 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}=1$ intersects the line $y=-x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087978 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "05138260-0471-5e01-b040-ffc1ad6ce57f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087978 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-x,$ we first replace $y$ with $-x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-x)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{5{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088752 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088752 #edb/ref 1061 464451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088752 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5524464b-6a66-5f98-893e-48ac0fedd44a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088752 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186088967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088753 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088753 #edb/ref 1061 464452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088753 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b342a9b4-8a39-5d74-9943-f197d4b9d913" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088753 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186087835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088754 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088754 #edb/ref 1061 464455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088754 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a3621b99-6383-5d05-94f4-a6d42a2480a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088754 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186087836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088755 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088755 #edb/ref 1061 464458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088755 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ff447adf-216a-5a29-bd4e-7b5990174906" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088755 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186088924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088756 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088756 #edb/ref 1061 464459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088756 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a34871c6-28d9-5cf8-8450-ec6fa81fe40e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088756 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186087837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088757 #edb/ref 1061 464462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088757 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "47213d7a-4e91-50f5-9a05-7fb5e4d396a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088757 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186087838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088924 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's now consider the hyperbola $\\dfrac {x^2}{9} - \\dfrac {y ^2}{3} = 1$ and the line $x = 6.$ The hyperbola and the line intersect at the points $A$ and $B,$ as shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/fa/fade29777e50e807aabb1f26f129669ae8b999235efb6c9bf72f11dcbfbb0a2e.png)\n\nTo find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line, we substitute the equation of the line, $x=6,$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{6}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{36}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ 4-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & =4-1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & =3 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ y & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the line $x=6$ at the points $\\left(6, \\pm3\\right).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088924 #edb/ref 1065 3495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088924 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d604b388-ae8e-5c3d-8061-34c0ded1ecc9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088924 #edb/ref 1067 "Finding Intersections of Hyperbolas and Lines" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088967 #edb/ref 1064 "The figure below shows the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{9} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25} = 1.$ We can see that this hyperbola intersects the $x$-axis at two points. How do we find the coordinates of these points?\n\n![](images/a3/a3f664f7e1916ca550c33060d78ad26e33aa9eb78ba32a44d46d7aa109ed4c2a.png)\n\nTo find the coordinates of the $x$-intercepts of a hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve the resulting equation for $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $(-3,0)$ and $(3,0).$" #edb/ref 1759