ref 17592186045417] [17592186294780 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f22d5e13-7b8e-592f-b5dc-bb0d54aed31e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294809 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186293917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294809 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294809 #edb/ref 1077 "field-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294809 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186293917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294809 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fa02b35d-22df-54f3-98bc-a4a4f0ca160c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294816 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186293708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294816 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294816 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294816 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186293708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294816 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fcc00e0b-6565-5a83-880f-674f914bedf0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294916 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294916 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294916 #edb/ref 1069 "q-277801" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294916 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294916 #edb/ref 1071 "The $x$-intercept of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}=1$ is$\\,(${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294916 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de2dc34f-1c0d-5c73-aef7-be1610303590" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294916 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16} & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x-1 & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $(1,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294730 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294984 #edb/ref 1069 "q-278353" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294984 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294984 #edb/ref 1071 "From **left to right,** the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}=1$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand \n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294984 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0916b8d4-936c-51d6-aa90-898aaf5837e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294984 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{(0-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18} & =2 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =36 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm 6 \\\\ x & =1\\pm 6 \\\\ x & =-5,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are $(-5,0)$ and $(7,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294987 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294987 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294987 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294987 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294987 #edb/ref 1069 "q-278363" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294987 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294987 #edb/ref 1071 "From **top to bottom,** the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $6{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2}=30$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand\n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294987 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "caf63029-110c-5e5e-ab8d-bb58a2ab4f5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294987 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =30 \\\\ 6{y}^{2}-5(0)^{2} & =30 \\\\ 6{y}^{2} & =30 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =5 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\sqrt{5})$ and $(0,-\\sqrt{5}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294988 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294988 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294988 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294988 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294988 #edb/ref 1069 "q-278364" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294988 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294988 #edb/ref 1071 "From **top to bottom,** the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}=1$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand\n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294988 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "80180fd4-af04-50e1-bba0-8e167a16e61a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294988 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(0)^{2}}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ (y-5)^{2} & =9 \\\\ y-5 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ y & =5\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,8)$ and $(0,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294992 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294992 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294992 #edb/ref 1069 "q-278371" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294992 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294992 #edb/ref 1071 "The hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1$ intersects the line $x=-3$ at\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294992 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0135d9ff-5368-56ef-b879-e7fafdfd541f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294992 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=-3,$ we substitute $x=-3$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the horizontal line $x=-3$ at $(-3,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294995 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186293962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294995 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294995 #edb/ref 1069 "q-278374" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294995 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294995 #edb/ref 1071 "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}=1$ intersects the line $y=x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294995 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "61ece0da-9c0b-5643-afdc-8f35ca2ac1ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294995 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{12{x}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{9{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-2$ and $x=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294998 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294998 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294215 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294998 #edb/ref 1069 "q-278379" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294998 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294998 #edb/ref 1071 "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola ${y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=20$ intersects the line $y=\\sqrt{5}x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294998 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e3924c5a-e5b9-5636-819e-461c9a4e5ffe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294998 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=\\sqrt{5}x,$ we first replace $y$ with $\\sqrt{5}x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ (\\sqrt{5}x)^{2}-{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-\\sqrt{5}$ and $x=\\sqrt{5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295001 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295001 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295001 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295001 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295001 #edb/ref 1069 "q-278384" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295001 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295001 #edb/ref 1071 "From **left to right**, the points where the hyperbola $4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=16$ intersects the line $y=2.5$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand\n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295001 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7096e183-2bac-525e-a16f-e109d122f25b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295001 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=2.5,$ we substitute $y=2.5$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 4(2.5)^{2}-{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 25-{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ -{x}^{2} & =16-25 \\\\ -{x}^{2} & =-9 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $y=2.5$  at the points $(-3,2.5)$ and $(3,2.5).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295003 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295003 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295003 #edb/ref 1069 "q-278387" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295003 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295003 #edb/ref 1071 "The hyperbola ${x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1$ intersects the line $x=1$ at\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295003 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c767294f-ea32-5b5b-87be-45853c02b18d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295003 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=1,$ we substitute $x=1$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ (1)^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $x=1$  at $(1,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345369 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\pm 3,1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345369 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345369 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02663bbe-2654-5af5-9b5b-4e8c4e1916cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345749 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\pm 1,1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345749 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345749 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2c8a94e6-9604-515d-86fc-d1c348b467d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345851 #edb/ref 1080 "$(-6,1)$ and $(2,1)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345851 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345851 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3a56a2bb-8115-5c70-ac47-863f5a1b19b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
